    <p>This analysis examines every winner of the Academy Award for Best Original Score from the 6th ceremony in 1934 through the 98th ceremony in 2026 — a span of <span class="highlight">93 award years</span>. The dataset contains <span class="highlight">93 films</span> and <span class="highlight">79 distinct individual composers</span>, several of whom appear multiple times as repeat winners.</p>
    <p>The Best Original Score category has undergone several transformations since its introduction. In its early years, the award recognized "Scoring" broadly, sometimes encompassing adaptations and arrangements alongside original composition. In certain periods, the Academy split the category into separate awards for dramatic scores and comedy/musical scores. This dataset consolidates to a single winner per year, providing a consistent longitudinal view.</p>
    <p>Notably, several winning entries credit multiple composers — seven ceremonies feature shared credit, from <em>Stagecoach</em> (1939, four composers) to <em>Soul</em> (2020, three composers). Each credited individual is counted as a winner for analytical purposes, which yields 79 unique composers across 93 ceremonies.</p>
